  "objects": [
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 14,
      "y": 46,
      "text": [
        "A fingerpost at the elbow of the road, and the newest board on it is a timetable.",
        "HARROWGATE HALT, ONE MILE WEST. DOWN TRAINS 06, 11, 15, 19.",
        "The old arm under it still says CART FERRY, and points at nothing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 18,
      "y": 24,
      "text": [
        "A board at the bridge foot, and a slot in the post under it.",
        "THE RHENE BRIDGE. TWELVE ARCHES. BUILT ON THE SUBSCRIPTION OF THE COUNTY.",
        "Below, smaller: FOOT, FREE. WHEEL, A PENNY. NOBODY SWIMS IT. ASK WHY LATER."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 18,
      "y": 8,
      "text": [
        "A milestone. AURELINE VI.",
        "This one is not moss-grown. Somebody scrubs it, and recently.",
        "The road here is wider than the road behind you, and it is wider again ahead."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 18,
      "y": 30,
      "text": [
        "A milestone. AURELINE XII.",
        "Cut into the base by a different chisel, later and in a hurry: HALT 1.",
        "A railway measures from its own stations. It does not care where the miles were."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 14,
      "y": 44,
      "text": [
        "A milestone. AURELINE XV.",
        "Somebody has counted the waggons past it and chalked the tally on the back.",
        "Two hundred and six since the light. All of them going the same way."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 31,
      "y": 61,
      "text": [
        "A milestone. AURELINE XVIII.",
        "A cart has clipped it at some point and the county has straightened it since.",
        "They straightened it. Nobody straightened a milestone on the Mire Road."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 11,
      "y": 25,
      "text": [
        "A signal, and a small board screwed to the mast at eye height.",
        "UP DISTANT. HARROWGATE. DO NOT PASS THE ARM.",
        "It is the only sentence out here addressed to somebody moving faster than you."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 45,
      "y": 13,
      "text": [
        "A dead branch line, and where it stops there is an arch bricked flat.",
        "THE OLD TUNNEL. CLOSED BY ORDER. THE HILL MOVED AND THE HILL WON.",
        "The brick is newer than the arch and older than anybody who could tell you why."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 44,
      "y": 40,
      "text": [
        "The wires leave the railway here and go east on their own poles.",
        "Ten of them, in a line, out across country with nothing at either end you can see.",
        "Somebody wanted to say something from somewhere quiet."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "script",
      "x": 8,
      "y": 15,
      "text": [
        "A gate either side of the line, and a plank between them, and a brass plate.",
        "OCCUPATION CROSSING. GRANTED IN PERPETUITY TO THE OWNER OF WEST FIELD.",
        "Somebody had eleven acres cut in half and this is what they got for it."
      ]
    },
